Description: log viewer for JSON and logfmt records
 hl reads structured logs -- JSON objects or logfmt lines, one record per line
 -- and renders them as readable columns, sorting by timestamp and colouring by
 level. It reads files, standard input, or several files merged together.
 .
 Records can be filtered on level, on time range, and on field values, which is
 what makes it usable on a log too large to page through. Output is plain text,
 so it composes with the rest of the shell.
